    "answer": {
      "short": "An even chance is a probability of 50%. Equally likely outcomes have the same probability as each other; it need not be 50%.",
      "worked": "An even chance means probability $\\frac{1}{2}$. Equally likely outcomes have equal probabilities, which need not be $\\frac{1}{2}$.",
